# Testing

Source: `governance/quality/testing.md`

For every change answer: which tests exist · which must be adapted (why) · which new tests are needed ·
which edge cases apply · what the regression risk is.

## Rules for AI-written tests
- No tautological tests (asserting mocks or constants).
- Never weaken assertions, broaden matchers, skip or delete tests to make a change pass.
  Changing an expectation needs a stated reason; disabling tests needs human approval.
- Test behaviour, not implementation details. Mock only at real boundaries. Keep tests deterministic.
- Bugfixes get a regression test that fails without the fix (where feasible).

```ts
// ❌ tautological
mockRepo.find.mockReturnValue(user); expect(mockRepo.find()).toBe(user);
// ✅ behaviour
mockRepo.find.mockReturnValue(inactiveUser); expect(() => service.login(inactiveUser.id)).toThrow(AccountInactiveError);
```

## Reporting
Report exact commands and real results. Tests not run are `not_run` with reason — never "passed".
Template: `templates/test-report.md` · Procedure: `skills/testing/SKILL.md`
